> mn(x: f32, y: f32) = asfloat(asuint(y) ^ ((asuint(x) ^ asuint(y)) & -(u32(asuint(x) < asuint(y)))))
  note: "^" between integers, next to bitwise operators: read as power, not xor (bitwise exclusive or) (write xor or ** to say which)
  note: '^' is power; use 'xor' or '⊕' for exclusive or
> mx(x: f32, y: f32) = asfloat(asuint(x) ^ ((asuint(x) ^ asuint(y)) & -(u32(asuint(x) > asuint(y)))))
  note: '^' is power; use 'xor' or '⊕' for exclusive or
> rmin(x: f32, y: f32) = min(x, y)
> rmax(x: f32, y: f32) = max(x, y)
> equiv mn ~ rmin
mn and rmin differ at 65536 points of the sample, e.g. x=-3.40282347e+38, y=-3.40282347e+38: 1.40129846e-45 vs -3.40282347e+38
> equiv mx ~ rmax
mx and rmax differ at 65536 points of the sample, e.g. x=-3.40282347e+38, y=-3.40282347e+38: 1.40129846e-45 vs -3.40282347e+38
> mnp(x: f32 in 0..1e30, y: f32 in 0..1e30) = asfloat(asuint(y) ^ ((asuint(x) ^ asuint(y)) & -(u32(asuint(x) < asuint(y)))))
  note: '^' is power; use 'xor' or '⊕' for exclusive or
> rminp(x: f32 in 0..1e30, y: f32 in 0..1e30) = min(x, y)
> equiv mnp ~ rminp
mnp and rminp differ at 65536 points of the sample, e.g. x=0, y=0: 1.40129846e-45 vs 0
